&lt;p&gt;Madonna's childhood home in Michigan has been placed on the market for a paltry $48,600 (£30,375).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pop superstar spent her youth in the four-bedroom Rochester Hills house with her parents and six brothers and sisters before relocating to New York in her search for fame and fortune.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Her family reportedly sold the property in 2001 for $270,000 (£168,750), but the home was ravaged in a fire in 2008 and has not been restored since, according to real estate blog Curbed.com.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;K2FeedTags&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Rochester Hills&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Detroit&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</summary>
